.”"}]}],"25340":[{"footnoteId":9576,"paragraphs":[{"pid":341,"text":"Or, “him.”"}]},{"footnoteId":9577,"paragraphs":[{"pid":342,"text":"Or, “immersion; dipping.” Gr., baʹpti·sma."}]}],"25352":[{"footnoteId":9578,"paragraphs":[{"pid":343,"text":"A denarius was a Roman silver coin that weighed 3.85 g (0.124 oz t)."}]}],"25362":[{"footnoteId":9579,"paragraphs":[{"pid":344,"text":"Or, “heralding.” Gr., ke·rysʹson; Lat., praeʹdi·cans."}]}],"25387":[{"footnoteId":9580,"paragraphs":[{"pid":345,"text":"“Gerasenes,” P75BDItVg; א, “Gergesenes”; ASyp,s, “Gadarenes.”"}]}],"25389":[{"footnoteId":9581,"paragraphs":[{"pid":346,"text":"An idiom; a repellent question indicating objection. See App 7B."}]}],"25392":[{"footnoteId":9582,"paragraphs":[{"pid":347,"text":"Or, “the deep.” See Ro 10:7."}]}],"25397":[{"footnoteId":9583,"paragraphs":[{"pid":348,"text":"Or, “had been saved.”"}]}],"25398":[{"footnoteId":9584,"paragraphs":[{"pid":349,"text":"See vs 26 ftn."}]}],"25403":[{"footnoteId":9585,"paragraphs":[{"pid":350,"text":"Or, “an only.” Gr., mo·no·ge·nesʹ. See Jg 11:34 ftn, “Child.”"}]}],"25405":[{"footnoteId":9586,"paragraphs":[{"pid":351,"text":"Or, “border; tassel.”"}]}],"25409":[{"footnoteId":9587,"paragraphs":[{"pid":352,"text":"Or, “has saved you.”"}]}],"25415":[{"footnoteId":9588,"paragraphs":[{"pid":353,"text":"Or, “wake up!”"}]}],"25416":[{"footnoteId":9589,"paragraphs":[{"pid":354,"text":"Or, “her breath (life-force).” Gr., to pneuʹma au·tesʹ; J17,18,22(Heb.), ru·chahʹ."}]}],"25424":[{"footnoteId":9590,"paragraphs":[{"pid":355,"text":"Or, “the tetrarch.” See 3:1 and ftns."}]}],"25435":[{"footnoteId":9591,"paragraphs":[{"pid":356,"text":"Or, “the disciples were with him.” B*, “the disciples came upon him.”"}]}],"25436":[{"footnoteId":9592,"paragraphs":[{"pid":357,"text":"Or, “the Immerser; Dipper.” Gr., ton Ba·pti·stenʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":9593,"paragraphs":[{"pid":358,"text":"Meaning “My God Is Jehovah.” J17,18,22(Heb.), ʼE·li·yaʹhu."}]}],"25440":[{"footnoteId":9594,"para